  "final_text": "All four steps are done, and I read the dashboard and rule back to confirm them.\n\n1. **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, id `90943e30-\u2026`) has time field `timestamp`. Main fields: `@timestamp`, `timestamp`, `clientip`, `bytes`, `response` (string, with a `response.keyword` subfield), `request`, `url`, `agent`, `host`, `geo.*`, `machine.*`, and `extension`.\n\n2. **Dashboard:** 'S4-c44c5ac6 Web logs' (id `bdcfec74-5fb5-4f90-9add-32ffbd4e1694`) has exactly two panels:\n   - \"Requests over time\": an ES|QL line chart, `COUNT()` bucketed by `@timestamp`.\n   - \"Requests by HTTP response code\": a donut chart, count split by `response.keyword` (top 20 terms).\n\n3. **Alert rule:** 'S4-c44c5ac6 5xx errors' (id `46e83a83-69a1-4994-8b8b-28e409136ecd`, type `.es-query`, consumer `alerts`).\n   - Checks every 1m.\n   - Counts documents where `response.keyword` is between `\"500\"` and `\"599\"`, over a 5m window on `timestamp`.\n   - Fires when the count is greater than 10.\n   - Created enabled.\n\n4. **Rename and read-back:** the donut panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". The dashboard read-back shows the title, two panels, and both panel titles. The rule read-back shows `enabled: true`.\n\nChoices I made:\n- The 5xx filter uses a string range on `response.keyword`. This is correct for three-digit codes, which is what the sample data uses. I didn't check the actual distinct values, because the Kibana ES and ESQL proxy endpoints aren't reachable from this API.\n- The line chart is ES|QL and the donut is data-view based, because the dashboard API validated those shapes.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
